<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Dec house material prices rise.</title>
<headline>Australian Dec house material prices rise.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian house building materials prices increased 0.1 percent in December from the previous month and were 0.3 percent higher than a year earlier, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.</p>
<p>Other building materials prices rose 0.2 percent in December and were 0.1 percent higher than a year before.  </p>
<p>The bureau said higher prices for structural timber was the main factor in the increase in the house building materials index.</p>
<p>&quot;This was partly offset by a small decrease in prices for clay brick,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The rise in the index for non-house materials was fuelled mainly by increases in prices for ready-mix concrete and non-ferrous pipes.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
